{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Mocking.</b> A term of idolatry, as it says ״וַיָּקֻמוּ לְצַחֵק״ (Exodus 32). Another interpretation: a term of uncovering nakedness, as you would say ״לְצַחֶק בִּי״ (Genesis 39). Another interpretation: a term of murder, as ״יָקוּמוּ נָא הַנְּעָרִים וִישַׂחֲקוּ לְפָנֵינוּ״ (II Samuel 2) — he would quarrel with Yitzchak over the inheritance and say, 'I am the firstborn and I take a double portion,' and they would go out to the field and he would take his bow and shoot arrows at him, as you would say ״כְּמִתְלַהְלֵהַּ הַיֹּרֶה זִקִּים״ (Proverbs 26), and he said, ״הֲלֹא מְשַׂחֵק אָנִי״ (Proverbs 26)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:44.860153350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}